# Source ranges for the MkDocs toolchain. The file that is INSTALLED is the
# compiled docs/requirements.txt beside it, which pins every direct and
# transitive distribution by version AND by hash (#1509); this one only says
# what the site is allowed to be built with.
#
# Regenerate after every edit here:
#
#     task docs:lock
#
# which is `uv pip compile docs/requirements.in --universal
# --python-version 3.14 --generate-hashes -o docs/requirements.txt`. 3.14 is
# the interpreter every consumer installs into, the release lane included: it
# builds and deploys on the runner since gh-plumbing v2.2.1. Before that it
# installed the set a second time inside `squidfunk/mkdocs-material:9.0.6`
# (CPython 3.11.0), which held the resolve at 3.11 and pymdown-extensions
# below 13 (#2908).
# EVERY ENTRY CARRIES A FLOOR AND A CEILING (#1601). NFR-009 §2.3.1 decides that
# §2.1 binds the COMPILE SOURCE of a class (a) list as well as the compiled
# output: the hashes below in docs/requirements.txt bind the bytes installed
# TODAY, and only the ranges here bind what the NEXT `task docs:lock` may
# choose. Without a ceiling that next run can pull a MAJOR of eight plugins at
# once, and the diff showing it is tens of kilobytes of hash lines nobody reads
# line by line. `src/backend/tests/unit/guards/test_docs_requirements_source_bounds.py`
# holds it.
#
# The ceilings added in #1601 are the currently resolved major of each package;
# raising one is a reviewed decision, which is the whole point.
#
# The FLOORS are the minor the site is built and tested with (#1615). Before,
# two of them sat a major or more below what resolved (mkdocstrings >=0.24.0 for
# 1.0.6, pymdown-extensions >=10.5 for 12.x) and so documented nothing. A floor
# here is a claim that `task docs:build` (strict) passed with that minor; raise
# it together with the recompiled lock and a strict build, never on its own.
mkdocs>=1.6,<2.0
mkdocs-material>=9.7,<10.0
mkdocs-static-i18n>=1.3,<2.0.0
mkdocstrings[python]>=1.0,<2.0.0
mkdocs-git-revision-date-localized-plugin>=1.6,<2.0.0
mkdocs-awesome-pages-plugin>=2.10,<3.0.0
mkdocs-minify-plugin>=0.8,<1.0.0
mkdocs-redirects>=1.2,<2.0.0
pymdown-extensions>=13.0,<14.0.0
mike>=2.2,<3.0.0
mkdocs-literate-nav>=0.6,<1.0
pyyaml>=6.0,<7.0
